Click Start → type: regedit:

HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\SecurityProviders\SCHANNEL\Protocols

Shows registry entries related to protocols SCHANNEL, i.e., TLS/SSL handling in Windows

In general, for security: 
SSL 2.0 / SSL 3.0 → disabled,  
TLS 1.0 / TLS 1.1 → preferably disabled, if legacy programs are not required,  
TLS 1.2 / TLS 1.3 → enabled.

Disable SSL 2.0 / SSL 3.0 / TLS 1.0 / TLS 1.1
Enabled = 0 
DisabledByDefault = 1

Enabling TLS 1.2 / TLS 1.3

Enabled 1
DisabledByDefault 0

